Pass the send tuple, not the address of the pointers to it, when a socket
error reports the destination unreachable. picoquic_packet_loop_do_udp_send
receives peer_addr and local_addr as pointers, so taking their address hands
picoquic_notify_destination_unreachable stack garbage: no path ever matches
and the notification is lost. A client whose local address disappeared then
never sees its path suspended, so it cannot migrate.

Introduced upstream by aee2b75d ("Refactor socket loop before testing QMux");
still present at 1d416567.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c.

diff --git a/picoquic/sockloop.c b/picoquic/sockloop.c
--- a/picoquic/sockloop.c
+++ b/picoquic/sockloop.c
@@ -2332,7 +2332,7 @@ int picoquic_packet_loop_do_udp_send(
 
             if (picoquic_socket_error_implies_unreachable(sock_err)) {
                 picoquic_notify_destination_unreachable(last_cnx, current_time,
-                    (struct sockaddr*)&peer_addr, (struct sockaddr*)&local_addr, if_index,
+                    (struct sockaddr*)peer_addr, (struct sockaddr*)local_addr, if_index,
                     sock_err);
             }
             else if (sock_err == EIO) {
